Z||000000||TooLowFiero||08-02-2000||11:11 PM||||i bout an 88 fiero coupe with a 5 speed 4cyl that was in a minor accident on the drivers side its needs from what ive noticed a strut spindle driver door and the door frame straightened out   is it worth to fix the car or part it out cuz if i part it out i plan on putting the nose and tail on my 85 se v6 4speed its a basic coupe no power options 120000 miles the tranny is a newer used tranny   what do you guys think? i only paid 100bucks for it <BR>TYIA<BR>Bobby<BR>aka TooLow||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||08-02-2000||11:47 PM||||<BR>is the fiero drivable? if so, i would possibly take it to a body shop and have them evaluate the damage. i think that will give you a better indication of the damage.<P>oh, and for what it is worth, if it isn't driveable, tow it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000002||TooLowFiero||08-03-2000||12:16 AM||||YES IT IS DRIVEABLE AND it was at a body shop and they said its not too bad but with the door frame being bent would cost a few bucks   the parts i can get and fix myself but i dont know how much the frame to get straightened out is gonna costyou can open the door but it is VERY hard to open the drivers side rear wheel is sitting at a slant but it was driven about 200 miles to get it home like that the door panel is junk as is the the part between the door and the wheel well i am thinking of fixing it but the idea of havingthe aero nose and tail is soo appealing &lt;snicker&gt; well all your input is taken into consideration and i hope i can find a happy medium plus i like the idea of owning an 88 fiero<BR>thanks all<BR>Bobby <BR>aka TooLow||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||08-03-2000||10:05 AM||||<BR>Regarding the nose on that 88, if you take it and the rear facia and place both on your 85 v6, you will basically have the equivalent to an 88 Formula, which is cool.<P>However, like you I am kinda in a quandry. I really don't like seeing any fiero parted out, if at all possible.  If the car is repairable and you have the money to do it, think of the story you can tell when you are finished, and the pride you will have in your ride.<P>Remember it is an 88 and 88's are rare, hence my leaning to keep it and work on it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||08-03-2000||11:17 AM||||Sounds all too familiar. By all means repair it!! I was in the same situation with my 88 coupe, and I couldn't be happier! Check it out:  <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=226077&a=1676320" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=226077&a=1676320</A> <P>Now if I could only get the V6 in!!<P>Oh yeah, if you need any suspension parts, LMK, there is an 88 in a junkyard near me!||||reg||1
